From 8ccfe3f9d229e4e946dab998969bb92403bdad14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:42:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/78] Port the Items screen of View Character

Port H065+$255A (items list with Ready/Use/Trade/Drop/Halve/Join/Sell/Id)
with $1C48 (can the item be given away), $1D80, $1E2C (halve), $1EE4
(join), $2C04 (ready/unready with the class, slot, hands and scroll
checks) and $2B2E (magic item effects, whose callees stay stubs). Also
port H063+$1BE8 (delete an item), H056+$0886 (debug trace), H033+$17E6
(is a scroll), H030+$0302 (word-wrapped text) and H044+$07DE (items
frame). Use, Trade, Sell and Id stay stubs.

The original passes the item list itself to the list menu (the first
$30 bytes of an item have the shape of a menu entry); the port builds a
mirror list of menu entries and maps the chosen entry back by position.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013G8KST8dgGfenpqx3RukYi
